// docs/specs/phase3/horses-and-carts.md 3.3: the fixed template vehicles of Phase 3 (no designer). rows: one character per cell, "_" empty; legend: the stack of parts in a cell, ground up.
// One cell is 1 m x 1 m, the world's own scale. Rows run from the rear (first) to the front (last: shafts, pole, traces); columns run across, so the number of characters in a row is the vehicle's width in metres.
// Wheels share a cell with the frame and the bed above them (two wheels of an axle are the two cells of a row, or a pair in one cell of a 1 m barrow). Real sizes: handcart 1 x 2 m, cart 2 x 5 m (3 m body, 2 m shafts),
// hay wain 2 x 7 m, ox wagon 2 x 8 m (5 m body, 3 m pole), covered wagon 2 x 7 m.
// Derived stats (mass, cargo kg and litres) are checked against the Phase 2 caravan vehicles (cart 500 kg / 1,000 L, ox wagon 1,000 / 2,000, handcart 150 / 300).
// P5-G (vehicle-designer 3.2): five more templates, the boats' rows run from the stern (first) to the bow (last). built_at is where they are built (a yard or a slipway); power lists how a boat moves.
// A boat's hull is every cell with hull planks; a keel gives it the fine lines of a rowing or fishing boat, a barge and a ferry are flat-bottomed. Hitch kind "tow" is a towing team on the bank (the tow post),
// "rope" a ferry hauled along its rope, "rowed" a boat that only its rowers move.
// hitch.slots is the animals of one team (a pair of oxen, one horse); hitch.max_animals is how many may be hitched in all (extra teams go in front, each pair pulling a tenth less than the last).
